erance"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The matrix–vector products each Lanczos run may spend; nil for 20,000 +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"20√n."}]}],"name":"maxIterations"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The eigenpairs, in order from that end of the spectrum."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thick-restart Lanczos (Wu–Simon) with full reorthogonalization and locking on M, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"fixed start vector; once k pairs are found, a run on the complement of their vectors checks"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that no copy of a multiple eigenvalue was missed. A Ritz pair is accepted when its residual"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance"},{"type":"text","text":" · max(|λ|, s\/1000), s Gershgorin’s bound on the spectrum; the vectors"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are then rotated by Rayleigh–Ritz on M, whose values are returned. The dense solver below 64"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, or when k is a third of them or more."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O((n + m) · products + n · k²) time, O(n · k) "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s for the vectors and n · max(30, 2k +"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10) for the basis."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","type":"